# Used when CEREBRO_DOMAIN is set: send plain-HTTP requests to HTTPS on the port the
# host actually publishes (CEREBRO_GATEWAY_HTTPS_PORT; 443 on a standard deployment).
# An explicit http:// site also stops Caddy from adding its own (port-443) redirect.
# `temporary` on purpose: browsers cache permanent redirects for good, which would trap
# anyone who later switches the gateway back to plain HTTP or changes the HTTPS port.
http://{$CEREBRO_DOMAIN} {
	redir https://{http.request.host}:{$CEREBRO_GATEWAY_HTTPS_PORT}{http.request.uri} temporary
}
